<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Civil Suit Plaint — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Code of Civil Procedure 1908 (Order VII Rule 1), Specific Relief Act 1963</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>Ad-valorem Court Fee as per Karnataka Court Fees and Suits Valuation Act 1958</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Filed before Senior / Junior Civil Judge Court</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Statement of Truth / Affidavit under Order VI Rule 15A CPC sworn before Oath Commissioner</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Civil Court having territorial and pecuniary jurisdiction over suit property</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>3 years for declaration / injunction under Limitation Act 1963</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Original Sale Deed / Khata Extract / Tax Receipts; Valuation Slip and Court Fee calculation memo; Vakalatnama duly executed in favor of Advocate</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">CIVIL SUIT PLAINT</div>
<div class="draft-body">IN THE COURT OF THE PRINCIPAL CIVIL JUDGE (SENIOR DIVISION) AT ________________________
O.S. NO. ___________ OF 2026

PLAINTIFF: ________________________________________, S/o ________________________________________
VERSUS
DEFENDANT: ________________________________________, S/o ________________________________________

SUIT FOR DECLARATION OF TITLE AND PERMANENT INJUNCTION
1. Plaintiff is absolute owner of Suit Property under registered sale deed dated ___/___/____.
2. Defendant has no right, title, or interest but attempted unlawful trespass on ___/___/2026.
3. Cause of action arose within jurisdiction of this Hon'ble Court.
PRAYER: Decree declaring Plaintiff absolute owner and permanent injunction restraining Defendant.

PLAINTIFF: ____________________________________     ADVOCATE: ____________________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>